  {
    "id": "c043",
    "name": "Loans to Related Parties — authority and conflicts",
    "text": "Loans to Related Parties The Company may make or invest in loans to persons or entities that are affiliated with the Manager, the Members, or the Servicer, such as a loan under which the borrower is owned by one or more of the members of the Manager, the Members, the Servicer or their family members (“Related Party Loans’). In cases of such Related Party Loans, conflicts of interest will exist between such Manager, Member, Servicer or its affiliated persons, on the one hand, and the Company, on the other, in connection with setting the terms of the loan and in connection with any enforcement action or renegotiation that may occur in the future. The Manager has undertaken to address these conflicts by applying the following standards and limitations to such Related Party Loans:"
  },
  {
    "id": "c044",
    "name": "Related Party Loans (a) — aggregate limit",
    "text": "(a) The aggregate principal amount of all Related Party Loans at any time shall not exceed 20% of total Company assets at such time;"
  },
  {
    "id": "c045",
    "name": "Related Party Loans (b) — terms and conditions",
    "text": "(b)} The terms and conditions of any Related Party Loans shall be consistent with the lending standards and policies set forth above and with loan terms typically offered by the Company on similar loans to unaffiliated borrowers; and"
  },
  {
