 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c119", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This provision routes borrower-paid fees and commissions to the Servicer, and to the Manager only where the Manager contracts directly with the Servicer, whereas Note Purchase Agreement §5.4(c)-(f) entitles the Manager to those amounts in all events. The entitlement to Commissions, Loan Fees and Documentation Fees is allocated differently by the two documents.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c120", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Loan Service Expenses are placed on the Servicer alone, while Note Purchase Agreement §5.5(a) says such expenses 'shall be borne by the Manager or the Servicer.' Which affiliate must absorb them if the Servicer does not is left unresolved.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.13}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c121", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The permission to take fees and equity interests in Portfolio Borrowers is made 'subject to restrictions with respect to Affiliated Transactions,' a capitalized term nowhere defined in the Memorandum. The only content for it lies in Note Purchase Agreement §5.7, to which this provision does not refer.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.21}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c122", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The sentence says the Company will be restricted 'in the amount of compensation it may receive,' but the Company pays rather than receives the compensation described throughout Section V (c110, c114, c119). The word 'receive' inverts the restriction it purports to summarise.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
